# ☀️ Automatic Solar Tracker using Arduino

An automated single-axis solar tracking system powered by Arduino. The system uses two Light Dependent Resistor (LDR) modules to continuously monitor ambient light levels and automatically rotates a solar panel via a servo motor toward the strongest light source, maximizing solar energy absorption throughout the day.

---

## 🛠️ Components Used

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|:---:|---|
| **Arduino Uno** | 1 | Microcontroller / Central Processor |
| **LDR Sensor Modules** | 2 | Detect light intensity (Left & Right) |
| **Servo Motor (SG90 / MG996R)** | 1 | Rotates the panel mechanism |
| **Breadboard** | 1 | Circuit prototyping without soldering |
| **Jumper Wires** | As required | Circuit interconnections |
| **Power Supply** | 1 | 5V DC power source (External 5V recommended for servo) |

---

## 🔌 Pin Connections & Circuit Wiring

### 1. LDR Modules to Arduino Uno

| LDR Module | Pin | Arduino Uno Pin | Connection Details |
|---|---|---|---|
| **LDR1 (Left)** | **VCC** | 5V | Common 5V Rail |
| | **GND** | GND | Common Ground Rail |
| | **AO** | **A0** | Analog Signal Output |
| **LDR2 (Right)**| **VCC** | 5V | Common 5V Rail |
| | **GND** | GND | Common Ground Rail |
| | **AO** | **A1** | Analog Signal Output |

---

### 2. Servo Motor to Arduino Uno

| Servo Pin | Wire Color | Connection |
|---|---|---|
| **Signal (PWM)** | Yellow / Orange | **Pin D9** |
| **Power (VCC)** | Red | External 5V Power Supply (*Recommended*) |
| **Ground (GND)**| Brown / Black | Common Ground (**Arduino GND + Power Supply GND**) |

> ⚠️ **Power Tip:** Powering the servo motor directly from the Arduino 5V pin can cause sudden voltage drops (brownouts) and reset the board. For best stability, power the servo using a dedicated 5V power source and tie the grounds together.

---

## ⚙️ How It Works

1. **Light Detection:** The two LDR modules constantly read light intensity on the left (`A0`) and right (`A1`) sides of the solar panel frame.
2. **Signal Comparison:** The Arduino calculates the difference between both sensor outputs (`error = leftValue - rightValue`).
3. **Thresholding (Deadband):** To prevent constant jittering, a threshold window (`deadband = 30`) is set.
4. **Servo Rotation:**
   * If the **left sensor** reads significantly higher light, the servo increments its angle to rotate **left**.
   * If the **right sensor** reads higher light, the servo decrements its angle to rotate **right**.
5. **Low-Light / Night Mode:** If both sensors detect darkness (`readings < 100`), the panel automatically returns to its flat neutral parking position (**90°**).

