## 💻 Arduino Code (`solar_tracker.ino`)

```cpp
#include <Servo.h>

Servo solarServo;

// Pin Definitions
const int ldrLeft = A0;   // Left LDR Module AO Pin
const int ldrRight = A1;  // Right LDR Module AO Pin
const int servoPin = 9;   // Servo Signal Pin

// Motor Settings
const int parkPosition = 90; // Neutral horizontal position (degrees)
int currentPos = 90;         // Active position tracker
const int deadband = 30;     // Hysteresis window to prevent motor jitter

void setup() {
  solarServo.attach(servoPin);
  solarServo.write(currentPos);

  pinMode(ldrLeft, INPUT);
  pinMode(ldrRight, INPUT);

  Serial.begin(9600);
  Serial.println("Solar Tracker System Initialized!");
}

void loop() {
  int leftValue = analogRead(ldrLeft);
  int rightValue = analogRead(ldrRight);

  // Calculate light differential
  int error = leftValue - rightValue;

  // 1. Low Light / Night Mode (Reset to 90 degrees)
  if (leftValue < 100 && rightValue < 100) {
    currentPos = parkPosition;
  }
  // 2. Left side is brighter -> Rotate Left
  else if (error > deadband) {
    currentPos = min(180, currentPos + 2);
  }
  // 3. Right side is brighter -> Rotate Right
  else if (error < -deadband) {
    currentPos = max(0, currentPos - 2);
  }

  solarServo.write(currentPos);

  // Serial Monitor Debugging
  Serial.print("Left LDR: "); Serial.print(leftValue);
  Serial.print(" | Right LDR: "); Serial.print(rightValue);
  Serial.print(" | Servo Angle: "); Serial.println(currentPos);

  delay(50); // Small delay for smooth mechanical motion
}

## Troubleshooting & Calibration
1. Jittering Servo: If the motor rapidly twitches back and forth, increase the deadband variable (e.g., change from 30 to 50) in the code.

2. Inverted Movement: If the panel turns away from the light source, swap the A0 and A1 LDR wires or swap the + and - rotation conditions in the code.

3. Common Ground: Always make sure your power supply GND and Arduino GND are connected together.
